The "Recomposing Modifiers" item in the next section labels `Modifier.offset { IntOffset(x, y) }` as bad, while its fix recommends exactly that lambda form. That item is under technical review. A correction is pending the owner's approval.

<!-- @after Common Misconceptions :: check -->
**Read the chain.** Decide before opening each answer.

<details><summary><code>Modifier.background(Red).clip(CircleShape)</code>: what shape is red?</summary>

A square. The background is outside the clip, so it paints its full rectangle; the clip affects only what comes after it. Put `clip` first.
</details>

<details><summary>Make a card with 8 dp of space outside its border and 16 dp inside.</summary>

`Modifier.padding(8.dp).border(1.dp, Gray).padding(16.dp)`: outer spacing before the border, inner spacing after it.
</details>

<details><summary>A <code>LazyColumn</code> inside <code>Column(Modifier.verticalScroll(state))</code> crashes.</summary>

The scrolling parent gives the lazy list an unbounded height, so it has no viewport. Flatten into one `LazyColumn`, or give the inner list a finite height.
</details>
